<https://wifire-data.sdsc.edu/dataset/feb5e09d-25a6-4303-931e-52934e70a0a3> <https://schema.org/datePublished> "2023-01-04T23:57:44+00:00" <urn:gleaner.io:eco:wifire:data:0a60fdc028a5b8a255b7705dc7691e52bb6acb88> .
<https://wifire-data.sdsc.edu/dataset/feb5e09d-25a6-4303-931e-52934e70a0a3> <https://schema.org/description> "<div><font size='4'>This is an export of the data archived from the 2022 National Incident Feature Service.<br />Sensitive fields and features have been removed.</font></div><div><font size='4'><br />Each edit to a feature is captured in the Archive. The GDB_FROM and GDB_TO fields show the date range that the feature existed in the </font><span style='font-size:large;'>National Incident Feature Service</span><font size='4'>.<br /><br /></font></div><div><font size='4'>The National Incident Feature Service is based on the National Wildfire Coordinating Group (NWCG) data standard for Wildland Fire Event. The Wildland Fire Event data standard defines the minimum attributes necessary for collection, storage and dissemination of incident based data on wildland fires (wildfires and prescribed fires). The standard is not intended for long term data storage, rather a standard to assist in the creation of incident based data management tools, minimum standards for data exchange, and to assist users in meeting the <a href='https://www.nwcg.gov/publications/pms936' target='_blank' rel='nofollow ugc noopener noreferrer'>NWCG Standards for Geospatial Operations (PMS 936)</a>.</font></div>" <urn:gleaner.io:eco:wifire:data:0a60fdc028a5b8a255b7705dc7691e52bb6acb88> .
